<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eleanor of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1241–1290</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eleanor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> was Queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> as the first wife of Edward I, whom she married in 1254. A daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III of Castile</a>, she inherited the county of Ponthieu from her mother in 1279. After her death in 1290 Edward raised the Eleanor crosses to mark the stages of her funeral procession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-castile.jpg" alt="Eleanor of Castile" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: History England Westminster abbey Souvenir book · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eleonora_by_Torel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
